  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Telegram",
      "text": "[English](README.en.md)\n\nDeepSeek Harness 的 Telegram 机器人插件，支持命令行版（Linux / WSL2 / macOS）和桌面版。在 Telegram 私聊中与 Agent 对话、发送图片和文件，并与 Web UI 共享工作区和会话。\n\n基于 **DeepSeek Harness v0.2.1-rc.3** 开发，通过 DSH 自带的 `dsh plugin` 安装。"
    },
    {
      "section": "安装",
      "text": "在终端运行（命令行版请先停止正在运行的 DSH）：\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IgnatAi401/dsh-telegram/main/install.sh | bash\n```\n\n脚本会自动找到本机的桌面版和命令行版并分别安装；macOS 上桌面版正在运行时会自动退出并在装好后重新打开。命令行版需要 Node.js 22.19+ 或 24+；桌面版如提示找不到 dsh 命令，先在 App 菜单的“管理 dsh 命令…”中安装。\n\nWindows 桌面版：在 App 的“插件”页点“添加插件”，填入 `github:IgnatAi401/dsh-telegram` 安装。Windows 上的命令行版请在 WSL2 中按上文安装。"
    },
    {
      "section": "配置与使用",
      "text": "1. 在 Telegram 中私聊 @BotFather 创建机器人，复制它给出的 Bot Token；私聊 @userinfobot 查看你的数字用户 ID。\n2. 启动 DSH（桌面版直接打开 App，命令行版运行 `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`），打开“插件”→ dsh-telegram，在页面上方填写 Bot Token 和允许的用户 ID（多个用逗号分隔），点“保存”。保存后立即生效，无需重启。\n3. 在 Web UI 配置模型凭据并创建工作区后，私聊机器人：\n\n- `/menu`：选择工作区，新建、打开或归档会话，切换模型和推理强度。\n- `/help`：查看可用命令。\n- 直接发送文字、图片或文件开始对话。\n\n仅支持私聊，只有允许的用户可以访问。同一个 token 不要同时运行多个机器人进程。旧版本写在 `~/.dsh/.env` 中的 `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`、`TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_IDS` 仍然有效，设置页中填写的值优先。"
    },
    {
      "section": "更新",
      "text": "重新运行安装命令即可，设置会保留。使用本地仓库时，先 `git pull` 再运行 `bash install.sh`。"
    },
    {
      "section": "卸载",
      "text": "```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IgnatAi401/dsh-telegram/main/install.sh | bash -s -- uninstall\n```\n\nWindows 桌面版在“插件”页卸载。卸载会一并删除插件页中保存的 Telegram 设置，保留 DSH、模型配置、工作区和历史记录。\n\n只想管理某个运行配置时，在命令末尾写上配置名，例如 `bash -s -- install desktop`；本地仓库中可运行 `bash install.sh [install|uninstall] [配置名]`。"
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH Telegram",
      "text": "[简体中文](README.md)\n\nA Telegram bot plugin for DeepSeek Harness, for both the command-line version (Linux / WSL2 / macOS) and Desktop. Chat with agents and send images and files in private Telegram chats, sharing workspaces and sessions with the Web UI.\n\nDeveloped against **DeepSeek Harness v0.2.1-rc.3** and installed through DSH's own `dsh plugin` command."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Run in a terminal (stop a running command-line DSH first):\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IgnatAi401/dsh-telegram/main/install.sh | bash\n```\n\nThe script finds Desktop and the command-line version on this machine and installs into each; on macOS a running Desktop is quit and reopened once the plugin is in place. The command-line version needs Node.js 22.19+ or 24+; if Desktop's dsh command is not found, install it first from the app menu (Manage dsh command…)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Windows Desktop: on the app's Plugins page choose Add plugin and enter `github:IgnatAi401/dsh-telegram`. For the command-line version on Windows, install inside WSL2 as above."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure and use",
      "text": "1. In Telegram, message @BotFather to create a bot and copy its token; message @userinfobot to see your numeric user ID.\n2. Start DSH (open the Desktop app, or run `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`), open Plugins → dsh-telegram, fill in the bot token and the allowed user IDs (comma-separated), and Save. The settings apply at once, without a restart.\n3. Configure model credentials and create a workspace in the Web UI, then open a private chat with the bot:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure and use",
      "text": "- `/menu`: select a workspace, create, open or archive sessions, and switch models and reasoning effort.\n- `/help`: list available commands.\n- Send text, images, or files to start chatting.\n\nOnly private chats and allowed users are supported. Do not run multiple bot processes with the same token. `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` and `TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_IDS` in `~/.dsh/.env` from earlier releases still work; values saved on the Plugins page take precedence."
    },
    {
      "section": "Update",
      "text": "Run the install command again; your settings are kept. For a local checkout, `git pull` first and then run `bash install.sh`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uninstall",
      "text": "```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IgnatAi401/dsh-telegram/main/install.sh | bash -s -- uninstall\n```\n\nOn Windows Desktop, uninstall from the Plugins page. Uninstalling also removes the Telegram settings saved on the Plugins page; DSH, model settings, workspaces, and history are preserved.\n\nTo manage a single profile, append its name, for example `bash -s -- install desktop`; from a checkout run `bash install.sh [install|uninstall] [profile]`."
    }
  ],
